  "note": "Complete principal Sanssouci palace exterior and attached side wings,north open paired-row curved colonnades with entablature/balustrades/urns,offset bowed south pavilion/copper dome with roof oculi/crown,long south window/herm rhythm,north giant order/entrance,round end bays,two end trellis gazebos and two low wing-front trellis walks. Separate New Chambers,Picture Gallery,windmill and broader vineyard terraces/fountains/gardens/optical interiors excluded. Native8m principal/child heights are generalized envelopes,not detailed cornice/dome heights. Original photo-proportional floor1.3m above51m approximate datum,eave9.1m,cornice9.55m,low roof10.3m,dome14.4m/crown15.05m. Colonnade entablature7.8..9.55m;individual column bases/plinth strips follow unchanged native field+.15m rather than raising the whole forecourt. Gazebos/trellises follow local field with original5.8m/4m envelopes. Exact historical thresholds,terrace/accessibility grades and vertical dimensions approximate. +X east and slightly north,-X west;+Z south toward vineyard terraces,-Z north forecourt/colonnades;+Y up. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
